<script>
'use strict';
$(() => {

  $('button.kata' ).click(() => cd.goto(cd.mountedPath('/choose_problem?type=kata')));
  $('button.group').click(() => cd.goto(cd.mountedPath('/choose_problem?type=group')));
  $('button.enter').click(() => cd.goto(cd.mountedPath('/enter')));

});
</script>

<div id="home-page">
  <div class="edged-panel heading">
    <div class="lockup">
      <table class="logo">
        <tr>
          <td><img src="/images/cyber-dojo.png"></td>
          <td class="cyber-dojo">cyber&#8209;dojo</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <div class="a-place-to-practise-programming">
        a&nbsp;place&nbsp;to&nbsp;<a href="https://blog.cyber-dojo.org/2015/05/do-more-deliberate-practice.html" target="_blank">practice</a>&nbsp;programming
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <% if @hostname == 'staging' %>
    <div class="edged-panel questions" style="background:red;">
    You are on https://<i><b><u>beta</u></b></i>.cyber-dojo.org <br/>
    These are <b><u>not</u></b> the pages you are looking for.<br/>
    Please go to <a href="https://cyber-dojo.org">https://cyber-dojo.org</a>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="edged-panel buttons">
    <button class="kata" type="button">
      <span class="fork-option-name">Practise solo</span>
      <span class="fork-option-note">Just you, your code and tests.</span>
      <ul>
        <li>No avatar</li>
        <li>No dashboard</li>
      </ul>
    </button>
    <button class="group" type="button">
      <span class="fork-option-name">Practise as a group</span>
      <span class="fork-option-note">A class or team practising together.</span>
      <ul>
        <li>Everyone gets an avatar</li>
        <li>One shared dashboard</li>
      </ul>
    </button>
    <button class="enter" type="button">
      <span class="fork-option-name">Enter existing</span>
      <span class="fork-option-note">Have a six-digit id?</span>
      <ul>
        <li>Join a group practice</li>
        <li>Drop back in where you left off</li>
      </ul>
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="edged-panel questions">
    <div class="question">
      Can you use cyber-dojo to get better at TDD?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      Yes, either individually or in a group training session.
      <ul>
        <li>
          this video explains how to use it for individual practice:
          <a href="https://youtu.be/lIRF8MgyXho" target="_blank">https://youtu.be/lIRF8MgyXho</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          this video explains how to use it for group practice:
          <a href="https://youtu.be/OGGk-iFVOPQ" target="_blank">https://youtu.be/OGGk-iFVOPQ</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      Is cyber-dojo free?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      It depends...
      <ul>
        <li>
          Using <code>https://cyber-dojo.org</code> in a commercial organization requires a licence
        </li>
        <li>
          Non-commercial use is free, but please donate
        </li>
        <li>
          100% of the licence fees and donations
          <a href="https://blog.cyber-dojo.org/2020/06/supporting-turing-trust.html"
             target="_blank">help children learn about software</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          The
          <a href="https://blog.cyber-dojo.org/2015/08/cyber-dojo-foundation.html"
            target="_blank">cyber-dojo Foundation</a>
            is a Scottish Charitable Incorporated Organisation<br/>
            <%= erb :'shared/donate_gbp_button' %>
            <%= erb :'shared/donate_usd_button' %>
            <%= erb :'shared/donate_eur_button' %>
		    </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      How much is a licence?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      It's up to you!
      <ul>
        <li>Large companies/organizations typically pay ~ £1000</li>
        <li>Smaller teams/individuals, less</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      How long does a license last?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      That's also up to you!
      <ul>
        <li>You can pay a larger amount once</li>
        <li>You can pay a smaller amount every year</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      How do I buy a licence?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      There are two ways:
      <ul>
		    <li>For larger corporations, email
        <a href="mailto:license@cyber-dojo.org?subject=I'd like to buy a cyber-dojo license please&body=...">license@cyber-dojo.org</a>
        with much you would like to pay, and how often, and we will raise an invoice
        </li>
        <li>Smaller businesses and individuals may prefer to pay directly via PayPal. See above
        </li>
        <li>Thank you</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      What about operational costs (such as cloud hosting)?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      They are generously paid by our sponsors:
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://kosli.com" target="_blank">Kosli</a>
          and CodeEntropy
        </li>
        <li>
          If you are interested in being a sponsor, please email
          <a href="mailto:sponsor@cyber-dojo.org?subject=I'm interesting in sponsoring cyber-dojo&body=...">sponsor@cyber-dojo.org</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      Why does cyber-dojo use animal avatars (drawn by <a href="https://www.behance.net/NadyaSivers" target="_blank">Nadya Sivers</a>)?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      Two reasons:
      <ul>
        <li>To provide identity without requiring a login</li>
        <li>To provide anonymity during reviews</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      Is cyber-dojo open-sourced?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      Yes. The repositories are split across four
      <a href="https://github.com" target="_blank">github</a> organizations:
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/cyber-dojo-start-points"
               target="_blank">cyber-dojo-start-points</a>
            holds the sets of initial source files
        </li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/cyber-dojo-languages"
               target="_blank">cyber-dojo-languages</a>
            holds the Dockerfiles for the images where the tests run
        </li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/cyber-dojo"
               target="_blank">cyber-dojo</a>
            holds the microservices for the server
        </li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/cyber-dojo-tools"
               target="_blank">cyber-dojo-tools</a>
            holds custom tools
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      Can I run my own cyber-dojo server?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      Yes. Instructions and scripts for running on...
      <ul>
        <li>
        <a href="https://blog.cyber-dojo.org/2016/10/running-your-own-cyber-dojo-server-on.html" target="_blank">Linux</a>
        </li>
        <li>
        <a href="https://blog.cyber-dojo.org/2016/10/running-your-own-cyber-dojo-server-on_15.html" target="_blank">Mac</a>
        </li>
        <li>
        <a href="https://blog.cyber-dojo.org/2016/10/running-your-own-cyber-dojo-server-on_34.html" target="_blank">Windows</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      What technologies does cyber-dojo use?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      <table>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby_(programming_language)"
               target="_blank">
              <img class="technology" src="/images/technologies/ruby.png">
            </a>
          </td>
          <td>
            <a href="https://github.com/cyber-dojo"
               target="_blank">
              <img class="technology" src="/images/technologies/github.png">
            </a>
          </td>
          <td>
            <a href="https://hub.docker.com/u/cyberdojo/"
               target="_blank">
              <img class="technology" src="/images/technologies/docker.png">
            </a>
          </td>          
          <td>
            <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AWS"
               target="_blank">
              <img class="technology" src="/images/technologies/aws.png">
            </a>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="name">ruby</td>
          <td class="name">github</td>
          <td class="name">docker</td>
          <td class="name">aws</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      Who are the
      <a href="https://blog.cyber-dojo.org/2015/08/cyber-dojo-foundation.html"
        target="_blank">cyber-dojo Foundation</a> trustees?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      <table>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <a href="https://jonjagger.blogspot.co.uk" target="_blank">
              <img class="trustee" src="/images/trustees/JonJagger.jpg">
            </a>
          </td>
          <td>
            <a href="https://www.kosli.com" target="_blank">
              <img class="trustee" src="/images/trustees/MikeLong.jpg">
            </a>
          </td>
          <td>
            <a href="https://olvemaudal.com" target="_blank">
              <img class="trustee" src="/images/trustees/OlveMaudal.jpg">
            </a>
          </td>
          <td>
            <a href="https://cucumber.io" target="_blank">
              <img class="trustee" src="/images/trustees/SebRose.jpg">
            </a>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="bio">
            <a href="https://jonjagger.blogspot.co.uk">Jon Jagger</a>
            is a software developer
            at <a href="https://www.kosli.com" target="_blank">Kosli</a>
          </td>
          <td class="bio">
            Mike Long is CEO
            at <a href="https://www.kosli.com" target="_blank">Kosli</a>
          </td>
          <td class="bio">
            <a href="https://olvemaudal.com" target="_blank">Olve Maudal</a>
            is a software guru at Equinor
          </td>
          <td class="bio">
            Seb Rose
            is an independent software consultant at
            <a href="https://claysnow.co.uk" target="_blank">claysnow.co.uk</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="question">
      What was the inspiration for cyber-dojo?
    </div>
    <div class="answer">
      In 2009 I (Jon) was consulting in Norway. A user-group organized an evening coding-dojo
      (in a local pub). An exercise, language, and test-framework was picked, and participants split
      into teams of about 5 people. After ~90 minutes everyone gathered for a review...
      <ul>
        <li>
        two teams had <em>nothing</em> to show since they were still trying to install
        the language and test-framework (using the pub wifi)
        </li>
        <li>
        the other teams spent a <em>long</em> <em>long</em> <em>long</em> time trying to connect
        their laptops to the projector (Linux, Mac, &amp; Windows)
        </li>
      </ul>
      I became convinced an online coding-dojo was a worthwhile project
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://blog.cyber-dojo.org/2015/05/do-more-deliberate-practice.html" target="_blank">practising</a> programming deserves more attention</li>
        <li>effective development is a
        <a href="https://jonjagger.blogspot.com/2013/10/teams.html" target="_blank">team</a> activity
        </li>
      </ul>
      I think there is real benefit in practising <em>outside</em> a professional IDE:
      <ul>
        <li>
          cyber-dojo is about
          <a href="https://jonjagger.blogspot.co.uk/2013/10/learning.html" target="_blank">learning</a>
          &mdash; an IDE about <em>development</em>
        </li>
        <li>
          cyber-dojo is for working
          <a href="https://jonjagger.blogspot.co.uk/2013/10/teams.html" target="_blank">together</a>
          &mdash; an IDE typically <em>alone</em>
        </li>
        <li>
          cyber-dojo aims to
          <a href="https://jonjagger.blogspot.co.uk/2014/02/improving.html" target="_blank">improve</a>
          <em>skills</em>
          &mdash; an IDE to <em>finish</em> <em>products</em>
        </li>
        <li>
          cyber-dojo promotes <a href="https://jonjagger.blogspot.com/2016/03/code-and-test-oppose-each-other.html" target="_blank">coding &amp; testing</a>
          &mdash; an IDE, mostly coding
        </li>
        <li>
          cyber-dojo helps you work <a href="https://jonjagger.blogspot.com/2013/12/time.html" target="_blank">slower</a>
          &mdash; an IDE <em>faster</em>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
